Title: Add qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview to models.yaml and the journal model set
Created: 2026-05-20
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-20T19:50Z claude created — discovered while running 0177; OpenRouter list confirmed availability.

--- body ---
## Context

The journal model set locked by ticket 0175 (`[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]`
in `experiments/experiments.toml:162-185`) pairs three `qwen3.6-*` siblings
(`27b`, `35b-a3b`, `plus`) with `qwen/qwen3-max` as the Qwen flagship.

This is internally inconsistent: the family's frontier entry is one generation
behind its mid-tier entries. The cause is an oversight in 0175 — at the time
of locking, the maintainer assumed `qwen3.6-max` was not yet on OpenRouter.

Verification (2026-05-20, during 0177 execution):

```
$ curl -s https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models | jq -r '.data[].id | select(test("qwen.*max"))'
qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview
qwen/qwen3-max-thinking
qwen/qwen3-max
```

`qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview` is live. Alibaba Model Studio confirms availability
(user-reported).

This means Experiment 1's "Qwen frontier" data point in the 0177 sweep is the
3-max model, not the 3.6-max-preview that would have been the architecturally
consistent choice within the family quartet.

## Impact

- **0177 results (current run)**: Qwen flagship is one generation behind its
  family siblings. Sweep results remain valid as a snapshot but should be
  annotated with this caveat in the manuscript (0178).
- **Experiment 2** ("deep research vs parametric" within-model claim,
  ticket-pipeline-mentioned at 0175): the intended within-family pairing is
  `qwen3-max` ↔ `qwen3-max-thinking`. If 0180 swaps to `qwen3.6-max-preview`,
  Experiment 2's Qwen entry stays on the 3-max generation for the within-model
  pair. Decide in 0180 whether the journal set becomes 17 models (add 3.6-max)
  or 16 with 3.6-max-preview replacing 3-max.

## Actions

1. Add `qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview` to `experiments/models.yaml` with verified
   prices from OpenRouter (`/api/v1/models`). Annotate provider, country (CN),
   architecture (likely MoE — confirm from model card), context window,
   size_class.
2. Decide between **augment** (16 → 17 models, both qwen3-max and
   qwen3.6-max-preview kept) and **replace** (swap qwen3-max for
   qwen3.6-max-preview). Augment is the safer default — preserves Experiment
   2's within-family pair, costs one extra 5-rep column (~$0.30).
3. Update `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]` accordingly.
4. Re-run the parametric baseline sweep (a new 0177-rerun ticket, or just the
   delta — 5 reps for the added/replaced model) so the 3.6 family is complete.
5. Note in the 0178 manuscript annex that the original 0177 run had the
   pre-fix configuration; flag the 0180 follow-up.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview` present in `models.yaml` with prices verified
- [ ] `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]` decision recorded in this ticket log
      (augment vs replace) with the reasoning
- [ ] Delta sweep run, 5 reps of the new model under `p1_base/`
- [ ] `measurements.jsonl` rebuilt; new rows visible with `prompt_version =
      "p1_base"` and `seed=42`
- [ ] 0178 manuscript annex notes the change

## Notes

- Discovered during 0177 (run-experiment-1-sweep). The 0177 mission spec
  explicitly forbade reconfiguring model IDs ("0175 locked them"), so the
  fix-up belongs in a separate ticket rather than mid-run.
- The four silent-drop fixes in commit bd46943 (model_set / seed / max_tokens
  / modules_dir) are a prerequisite for any future sweep against this set,
  whether or not 0180 swaps the Qwen flagship.
- "preview" suffix: OpenRouter sometimes deprecates `:preview` slugs once a
  GA variant ships. Worth checking quarterly; if `qwen/qwen3.6-max` (no
  preview) lands, switch to that in the same ticket cycle.
